<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<PackageId>TmEssentials</PackageId>
		<Version>2.9.0</Version>
		<Authors>BigBang1112</Authors>
		<Description>A .NET library providing essential Trackmania features, like the time or text formatting.</Description>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Petr Pivoňka</Copyright>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/BigBang1112/tm-essentials</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageIcon>logo_icon_outline.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>trackmania, tm, essentials, maniaplanet, time, account, formatting</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
- **Breaking:** `TimeInt32` conversions from `TimeSpan` and `TimeSingle` are now explicit, so they need a cast
  - `(TimeInt32)timeSpan` truncates to whole milliseconds and throws `OverflowException` outside the `TimeInt32` range (about ±24.8 days)
  - `(TimeInt32)timeSingle` rounds to the nearest millisecond, like `TimeSingle.ToTimeInt32()` and `TimeInt32.Add(ITime)` with a `TimeSingle`
- **Breaking:** `TimeInt32` arithmetic throws `OverflowException` instead of wrapping around, like `TimeSpan`
  - Applies to the `+`, `-` and `*` operators, `Add`, `Multiply(int)`, `Negate`, `Duration` and the constructors with days, hours, minutes and seconds
- **Breaking:** `TimeInt32.FromDays`, `FromHours`, `FromMinutes`, `FromSeconds` and `FromMilliseconds` round to the nearest millisecond, like `TimeSpan` on .NET Framework, instead of truncating
  - For example, `TimeInt32.FromSeconds(0.251f)` is now 251 milliseconds instead of 250
  - They and `FromTicks` throw `OverflowException` outside the `TimeInt32` range instead of returning a wrong time, and `ArgumentException` for NaN
- **Breaking:** `TextFormatter.Deformat`, `FormatAnsi` and `FormatHtml` now read formatting codes the same way as ManiaPlanet, so some results differ from 2.8.0
  - Added 1 and 2 digit colors (`$f` is `$f00`), `$p` manialinks, the `$[` and `$]` escapes, and `$m` for normal width
  - `$&lt;` and `$&gt;` save and restore up to 7 styles, and `$z` and `$g` reset to the style saved by `$&lt;`
  - Carriage returns and a trailing `$` are removed
- **Breaking:** `MapUtils.GenerateMapUid` overloads now generate UIDs the same way as the game, so UIDs from a seed differ from 2.8.0 and some UIDs are shorter than 27 characters
- **Added `MapUtils.GenerateMapUid(Guid, uint)` and `MapUtils.TryDecodeMapUid`** to make a map UID from a UUID and a CRC32 like the game, and to read them back from a UID
- **Added Font Awesome 4.7 icon support** to `TextFormatter.FormatHtml` with an `iconCssClass` parameter that wraps icon characters in `span` elements of that class
  - Added `TextFormatter.IsFontAwesomeIcon`
- Added `TextFormatter.FormattingCodeRegexPattern` that matches one formatting code the same way as the formatters when no link is open
- **Fixed `TextFormatter.FormatHtml` links that could run scripts.** `$l` links keep `http` and `https` URLs, add `http://` to URLs without a scheme, and are not clickable with any other scheme like `javascript:`
  - Whitespace around link URLs is trimmed like in the game
- Fixed `TextFormatter.FormatAnsi` ignoring 1 and 2 digit color codes, `$&lt;`, `$&gt;` and `$t`
- Fixed `TimeSingle.ToString` writing some times one millisecond lower, for example `0:00.250` for 0.251 seconds
- Fixed `TimeInt32.Days`, `Hours`, `Minutes`, `Seconds` and `ToString` losing precision near the end of a day or an hour
- Changed `TimeInt32` equality and comparison with `TimeSingle` and other `ITime` values to use `TotalSeconds`, so `new TimeInt32(251) == new TimeSingle(0.251f)`
- Fixed `AccountUtils.ToAccountId` returning an account ID for logins that do not decode to exactly 16 bytes. It now throws `FormatException`
- Improved performance and reduced allocations, for example time parsing is up to 12 times faster, map UIDs up to 14 times faster and `TextFormatter.FormatHtml` up to 19 times faster
- Removed the `totmstring` native entry point
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net9.0;net8.0;netstandard2.1;netstandard2.0;net462</TargetFrameworks>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<LangVersion>14</LangVersion>
		<IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
		<IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

		<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
		<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
		
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<DocumentationFile>bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\$(AssemblyName).xml</DocumentationFile>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="../../logo_icon_outline.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>
    
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' OR '$(TargetFramework)' == 'net462'">
        <PackageReference Include="System.Memory" Version="4.6.3" />
    </ItemGroup>
	
	<ItemGroup>
		<Using Remove="System.Net.Http" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="$(AssemblyName).Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="$(AssemblyName).Benchmarks" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>